            <h2>5 Daily Habits to Fix Desk Posture &amp; Reduce Work Burnout</h2>
            
            <h3>1. The 20-20-20 Rule for Digital Eye Strain</h3>
            <p><strong>Answer Summary:</strong> To prevent digital eye strain during long computer sessions, look at an object 20 feet away for at least 20 seconds every 20 minutes. This relaxes the ciliary muscles in your eyes and reduces visual fatigue.</p>
            
            <h3>2. Ergonomic Monitor Alignment</h3>
            <p><strong>Answer Summary:</strong> Position your primary monitor so the top third of the screen sits at eye level, roughly an arm's length away. This prevents forward head tilt and reduces cervical spine tension.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            
            <h3>How does a 10-minute walk lower stress?</h3>
            <p>A brief 10-minute brisk walk reduces circulating cortisol (stress hormone) levels while triggering endorphin release, boosting focus and mental clarity.</p>
